# Production / staging secrets - NAMES ONLY (ADR-019). Never put a value in this file.
#
# Each name is one file in the host secrets directory (default /etc/lms/secrets,
# directory 700, files 600, owned by root), mounted into the containers at
# /run/secrets/<NAME> by infrastructure/docker-compose.prod.yml.
# How to create, back up and rotate them: docs/operations/production-secrets-runbook.md
#
# Columns: NAME | required? | how to generate | used by | if missing
#
# --- Critical: the backend refuses to start without these (ProductionSecretsStartupValidator)
DB_PASSWORD                          | required | openssl rand -base64 24            | backend, postgres | backend and database do not start
JWT_SECRET                           | required | openssl rand -base64 48            | backend           | backend does not start
MEDIA_CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY     | required | openssl rand -base64 32 (32 bytes) | backend           | backend does not start; LOSING it = every media connection must reconnect
PAYMENT_CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY   | required | openssl rand -base64 32 (32 bytes) | backend           | backend does not start; LOSING it = every tenant PayHere account must be re-entered
#
# --- Required by the compose stack
REDIS_PASSWORD                       | required | openssl rand -base64 24            | backend, redis    | Redis does not start
#
# --- Feature secrets: the feature fails closed (503 / "not available") while missing
VIDEO_PLAYBACK_TOKEN_SECRET          | required for video playback | openssl rand -base64 48 | backend | secure video playback returns 503
PAYMENT_GATEWAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET       | if a payment gateway webhook is used | from the gateway / openssl rand | backend | gateway webhooks rejected
LIVE_CLASS_PROVIDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET   | if the fake live-class provider webhook is used | openssl rand -base64 32 | backend | its webhooks rejected
ZOOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET_TOKEN            | for Zoom | Zoom app > Feature > Event subscriptions "Secret Token" | backend | Zoom webhooks rejected
ZOOM_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET             | for Zoom | Zoom Marketplace app credentials | backend | Zoom shows "not available"
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET           | for YouTube | Google Cloud OAuth client (web application) | backend | YouTube shows "not available"
VIMEO_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET            | for Vimeo | Vimeo developer app | backend | Vimeo shows "not available"
OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY            | for uploads/materials | object storage provider | backend | object storage unavailable
MAIL_PASSWORD                        | for email | Google "App Password" (16 chars) | backend | emails fail to send
#
# Non-secret settings (image tags, PLATFORM_DOMAIN, OAuth client IDs, storage endpoint, mail
# username, ...) are NOT secrets: they go in the non-secret env file passed with --env-file.
